sentences.l:
and down ran wet sweat,
and close-set weals along ribs and shoulders
with blood crimson ran up;

As second in turn lifted him much-enduring, heavenly Odysseus,
and he moved him a little from the earth, but no more lifted him,
and in he bent a knee;

So he spoke, and rose at once swift Ajax, son of Oileus,
and up many-wiled Odysseus, and then Nestor’s son
Antilochus;
